{"agent":"mcpskew-kilo","data":{"budget":"","claim":"Config._is_code_tree decides the config loader's strictness by PATH alone; a long-lived MCP server running from the source tree (editable install / .ddflow/local/bin/ddflow) has root == _CODE_TREE, reads a config file STRICTLY after the tree is bumped (0.2.10 -> 0.2.11), and raises 'unknown knob lease.reconcile_tests' on a knob the running code predates, where it should be greyed/warned.","falsifier":"If comparing the frozen running ddflow.__version__ against on-disk declared_version(_CODE_TREE) and treating a mismatch as not-the-code-tree (lenient) turns the raise into unknown_knobs recording, CONFIRMED; if the loader still raises with the comparison in place, REFUTED.","item":"B-mcp-shell-version-skew","mechanism":"ddflow/config/_core.py:186 sets lenient=not _is_code_tree(root); _is_code_tree is path equality only, so a stale process still satisfies it while its frozen ddflow.__version__ is the OLD release: the same-commit assumption breaks and the loader raises instead of greying.","probe":"tests/test_mcp_shell_version_skew.py::test_a_stale_code_tree_greys_an_unknown_knob_not_raise (declared=0.2.11, running=0.2.10, root==_CODE_TREE): greyed now, would raise without the fix; the guard test (running==declared) still raises.","probe_output":"5 passed in 1.17s (test_mcp_shell_version_skew.py)","question":"Why does an MCP tool such as ddflow_next raise 'unknown knob lease.reconcile_tests' when a long-lived MCP server predates a bumped source tree, and would making _is_code_tree version-aware grey it instead?","sources":[],"verdict":"CONFIRMED"},"id":"e708a68843d0de34a4f8995d7","kind":"research.recorded","lamport":174138,"schema":1,"subject":"Rfd38a4800c","ts":"2026-11-11T13:06:09.735398Z"}
{"agent":"mcpskew-kilo","data":{"by":"mcpskew-kilo","evidence":{"diff_stat":{"deletions":3,"files":3,"insertions":135,"untracked":1},"note":"Research Rfd38a4800c CONFIRMED. Probe: $HOME/src/ddflow/.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/test_mcp_shell_version_skew.py -q -> 5 passed in 1.17s. The version-aware _is_code_tree turns the stale-code-tree unknown-knob raise into unknown_knobs greying; the guard test proves a fresh (running==declared) tree stays strict.","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/config/_tree.py":"100644 a0a51103020d8523ee52e1844662c0a0d30ffe27","ddflow/services/upgrade_notice.py":"100644 2c8c4b048dc7e54b50412492e3f5a04e9cc0317e","tests/test_mcp_shell_version_skew.py":"100644 10ce69d193457d3ccc37e96cffb91a651e9fc05c"},"tree_sha":"c9144336d48c+st:89d8fdc57a12b096ed651525234abad4"},"gate":"research","reason":""},"id":"e63ec8662d632b0d368487e44","kind":"gate.passed","lamport":174150,"schema":1,"subject":"B-mcp-shell-version-skew","ts":"2026-11-11T13:07:18.069292Z"}
{"agent":"mcpskew-kilo","data":{"by":"mcpskew-kilo","evidence":{"diff_stat":{"deletions":3,"files":3,"insertions":135,"untracked":1},"note":"Rule bearing on this task: the layering rule (tests/test_layering.py) -- config imports nothing, services may import config+infra. ddflow/config/_tree.py adds stdlib-only (re, sys, pathlib) and imports no ddflow layer (verified by tests/test_layering.py::test_a_module_imports_only_from_below, which passed). ddflow/services/upgrade_notice.py imports ..config._tree (below services) + ..infra (below services), both allowed. D-compat / config-newer-than-code (Bcfc0d22a09, B9cb7dd1c3b) is the compat contract this change extends to a stale source-tree MCP server.","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/config/_tree.py":"100644 a0a51103020d8523ee52e1844662c0a0d30ffe27","ddflow/services/upgrade_notice.py":"100644 2c8c4b048dc7e54b50412492e3f5a04e9cc0317e","tests/test_mcp_shell_version_skew.py":"100644 10ce69d193457d3ccc37e96cffb91a651e9fc05c"},"tree_sha":"c9144336d48c+st:89d8fdc57a12b096ed651525234abad4"},"gate":"rules","reason":""},"id":"e0df7c5937c4b601f55743484","kind":"gate.passed","lamport":174169,"schema":1,"subject":"B-mcp-shell-version-skew","ts":"2026-11-11T13:07:46.335114Z"}
