{"agent":"mcpskew-kilo","data":{"by":"grok-4.7","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"`declared_version` only turns `OSError` into `\"\"`. `Path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")` raises `UnicodeDecodeError` (a `ValueError`) for a code tree whose `ddflow/__init__.py` is not valid UTF-8, or if the file uses a non-UTF-8 coding cookie. That exception is not caught in `_is_code_tree`, so a same-path check that used to return a bool now aborts config loading. The same exception escapes into `installed_version`: the `or info.version` fallback never runs, the bare `except Exception` returns `\"\"`, and a source-tree/editable install whose metadata version was already known (for example `0.2.11`) is reported as having no installed version.","digest":"71f3e885fba89c3c","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/config/_tree.py:declared_version","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/config/_tree.py:declared_version"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"The renamed-intent test now writes `b\"x = 1\\n\\xff\\n\"`. That byte is not valid UTF-8, so `declared_version` returns `\"\"` from the new `(OSError, ValueError)` handler and never reaches `_VERSION_LINE`. A tree whose `__init__.py` is valid UTF-8 and simply has no version literal (the case the name still claims) is no longer exercised; if `return found.group(1) if found else \"\"` were dropped, this test would still pass.","digest":"69fe043ff9156181","family":"xai","location":"tests/test_mcp_shell_version_skew.py:test_declared_version_is_empty_when_the_tree_has_no_literal","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"LOW","title":"tests/test_mcp_shell_version_skew.py:test_declared_version_is_empty_when_the_tree_has_no_literal"}],"chunks_total":1,"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_findings":1,"delta_from":"d433ce95d3ee521590000338ed690f526e33b981","delta_raised":["69fe043ff9156181"],"delta_rounds":1,"diff_chars":1951,"diff_sha":"81ebb5012b3b0225044b15b78d6e77e9e2670f009c073a7dfb86f34311d226fe","d