{"agent":"mcpskew-kilo","data":{"digest":"69fe043ff9156181","finding":2,"gate":"critic","location":"tests/test_mcp_shell_version_skew.py:test_declared_version_is_empty_when_the_tree_has_no_literal","probe":"The finding is right: the first cut merged the 'valid UTF-8, no literal' case into the non-UTF-8 case. tests/test_mcp_shell_version_skew.py now separates them: test_declared_version_is_empty_when_the_tree_has_no_literal writes x = 1 (valid UTF-8, no __version__), and test_declared_version_is_empty_for_a_non_utf8_file writes b'__version__ = \"\\xff\"\\n'.","severity":"LOW","title":"tests/test_mcp_shell_version_skew.py:test_declared_version_is_empty_when_the_tree_has_no_literal","verdict":"confirmed"},"id":"ec026c62ae7422ea4caf1b241","kind":"review.triaged","lamport":174350,"schema":1,"subject":"B-mcp-shell-version-skew","ts":"2026-11-11T13:23:47.981746Z"}
